%N A235001 Odious squares.
%C A235001 This sequence is the intersection of A000069 and A000290.
%C A235001 Numbers k^2 such that A159918(k) is odd.
%H A235001 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A235001/b235001.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a> (terms 1..1000 from Harvey P. Dale)
%F A235001 a(n) = A235331(n)^2. - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 16 2026
%e A235001 16 is a square 4^2 and 16 in base 2 is a 10000, having an odd number of 1's, thus 16 is in this sequence.
%t A235001 Select[Range[75]^2,OddQ[DigitCount[#,2,1]]&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Jan 14 2014 *)
%o A235001 (PARI) isok(k) = issquare(k) && hammingweight(k) % 2 == 1; \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 16 2026
%Y A235001 Cf. A000069, A000290, A159918, A231431 (evil squares), A235331.
